    "response": "{\"decision\":\"no_flaw_established\",\"issues\":[{\"category\":\"contextual_flattening\",\"target_kind\":\"assertion\",\"claim_quote\":\"The displayed sources show that policy debate is mainly driven by institutional procedures and formal paperwork.\",\"evidence\":[{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_1edf53ce09cb2790\",\"quote\":\"My Lords, as always, the noble Lord asks a very good and detailed question, and I will follow up in writing—but £125 million of the £1 billion growth deal recently announced is addressed to skills capital, and a further £26 million to particular apprenticeships. By bringing business and local authorities together, and by looking at growth and what is needed—skills represent a…\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_cbc69161c2f91af8\",\"quote\":\"My Lords, I welcome the Statement and congratulate Sir Robert once again on his most thorough analysis. I also welcome the long overdue proposed change in the law to make employers responsible if whistleblowers are harassed. Does the suggested new duty of candour mean that never again will we see gagging clauses in any NHS contractual arrangements?…\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_f4de7c9424eb2206\",\"quote\":\"My Lords, I understand that my noble friend was responding to Amendment 4, in which case I apologise.\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_73c2800f732dcebd\",\"quote\":\"There are signs of people both downsizing and going into work on a policy that was designed to save the state £0.5 billion a year and is doing so. One of the side-effects that is not properly appreciated is the extraordinary change in the numbers in social housing who are out of work. They have now reached the lowest levels that we have ever recorded.”}],\"\n    }],\"whole_packet_no_support\":\"No specific evidence directly supports the claim that policy debate is *mainly* driven by institutional procedures and formal paperwork.\",\"mechanism\":\"The sources discuss various policy initiatives, funding allocations, and impacts on social housing, but do not establish a primary driver of debate.\",\"material_consequence\":\"The claim oversimplifies the complex factors influencing policy debate, potentially ignoring stakeholder engagement and broader societal concerns.\",\"counterconditions\":\"The evidence highlights diverse elements, including financial allocations, skills development, and welfare impacts, suggesting a multi-faceted debate.\"}\n    ],\"unresolved\":[],\"rationale\":\"The provided evidence focuses on specific policy areas and responses, lacking a broad assessment of the *main* drivers of policy debate. The claim requires a more comprehensive analysis beyond the presented excerpts.\"}",
    "done": true,
